        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Couples Therapy &amp; Relationship Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1"><h2>Old patterns that awaken in the relationship</h2><p>In partnerships we can have wonderful experiences: feeling accepted, valued and closely connected. At the same time, our closest relationships also activate our deeply rooted patterns. Dealing with this is not easy – for ourselves and for the people we love. Under tension, hurt or protective inner parts often take the wheel: we complain or get loud, withdraw, justify ourselves or give in. Although at heart we are seeking connection, we feel misunderstood and treated unfairly. Our reactions run lightning-fast and involuntarily, and the dynamic we create together is hard to resolve alone.</p></div>
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c2"><h2>My approach: understanding and changing patterns</h2><p>We explore which parts become active in conflicts, where they come from and what they want to protect. We make visible what remains unspoken in everyday life, and translate reproaches into concerns:</p>
            <div class="rd-kernsatz"><p>What do I need, what do you need, what can we agree on together?</p></div>
            <p>In doing so, we distinguish between what you can give yourselves and what you wish for from the other person. Each person takes responsibility for their own parts.</p>
            <p>We clarify how you can approach each other again after an argument. Even within the sessions, understanding and appreciation can arise again, and we develop ideas for how to carry this into everyday life. Joint sessions are central. If needed, individual sessions are also possible after clear agreements.</p>
            <button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button>
            <p class="rd-keep"><a class="rd-more-link" href="{{ '/en/systemische-therapie/' | url }}#arbeitsverstaendnis">More on my systemic professional understanding<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-ez rd-ez-lists rd-mtabs" id="anlaesse" data-index="2">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Couples Therapy &amp; Relationship Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-mtabbar" role="tablist"><button class="is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mtab="0">Occasions</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mtab="1">How it helps</button></div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1 rd-mpanel is-active" data-mpanel="0"><h2>What can be occasions for couples therapy?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>Arguments, the unspoken or boundary violations shape the relationship</li>
              <li>One person feels ignored, rejected, confined or controlled</li>
              <li>Life changes burden the relationship: children, blended family, career upheavals, moving, finances</li>
              <li>Trust has been lost: secrets, disloyalty, affairs</li>
              <li>Values, role models or ideas about relationships seem hard to reconcile, for example in the case of cultural differences or disagreement about opening the relationship</li>
              <li>Thoughts of separation in everyday life, or a separation that is not yet complete</li>
              <li>Crises, illness, loss or grief affect the relationship</li>
            </ul></div>
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c2 rd-mpanel" data-mpanel="1"><h2>What can couples therapy help with?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>Recognizing recurring patterns and understanding your own part in the shared dynamic</li>
              <li>Understanding where reactions come from and what they want to protect</li>
              <li>Recognizing and expressing your own feelings and needs and those of the other person more clearly</li>
              <li>Reacting more consciously in conflicts and staying in contact in order to understand each other better</li>
              <li>Finding a good way of dealing with an impending separation</li>
              <li>Experiencing more closeness, lightness and satisfaction in everyday life again</li>
            </ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

